Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: enable MMU interrupts during device initialization

Backport the init-time interrupt enablement from Adrián Larumbe's upstream
"drm/panfrost: Explicitly enable MMU interrupts at device init" to BSP 6.1.
Upstream: https://lore.gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm-ai-reviews/20260604-claude-fixes-v2-7-57c6bd4c1655@collabora.com/

Panfrost starts runtime-active. Its initial MMU setup only registers the
interrupt handler; the mask is enabled on reset/resume. With autosuspend
disabled, the first tiler-heap page fault is never serviced and the first
GNOME vertex/tiler job times out. Enable interrupts before accepting jobs.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
@@ -768,6 +768,9 @@ int panfrost_mmu_init(struct panfrost_device *pfdev)
 		return err;
 	}
 
+	mmu_write(pfdev, MMU_INT_CLEAR, ~0);
+	mmu_write(pfdev, MMU_INT_MASK, ~0);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
